From: aurelex <aurelex@localhost>
Date: Sun, 31 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] android carve: no QGuiApplication; writable config home

Three related carve fixes so the engine runs in a plain Android app (no
QtActivity, no QGuiApplication / platform plugin):

- dictionary.cc getOptimalIconSize(): it read qGuiApp->devicePixelRatio(),
  which required a GUI application. Return the fixed 64 base (icon
  rendering is cosmetic).
- tiff.cc tiff2img(): called QApplication::primaryScreen(), which crashes
  with only a QCoreApplication. Guard on a null screen and fall back to the
  image's own size (the TIFF path is rare; it must not crash).
- config.cc getHomeDir(): on Android the XDG branch resolves via
  QStandardPaths, which needs a QtApplication to guarantee a writable dir,
  and aborted with "Can't use home directory to store GoldenDict
  preferences". Use the HOME env var (the boundary sets it to the app's
  private files dir) on Android and keep .goldendict there.

With these, gd_init constructs a plain QCoreApplication on Android (design
D2's original "stub the GUI code" intent), no Qt platform plugin needed.

---
 src/config.cc          | 14 ++++++++++++++
 src/dict/dictionary.cc |  2 +-
 src/tiff.cc            |  5 +++--
 3 files changed, 17 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/config.cc b/src/config.cc
index 29e62f54..b4272739 100644
--- a/src/config.cc
+++ b/src/config.cc
@@ -2225,6 +2225,19 @@ QDir getHomeDir()
 
   QDir result;
 
+#ifdef Q_OS_ANDROID
+  // On Android there is no conventional HOME and QStandardPaths (via XDG)
+  // needs a QtApplication to resolve to a guaranteed-writable dir. The
+  // boundary sets HOME to the app-private files dir; use it directly.
+  const QByteArray home = qgetenv( "HOME" );
+  if ( !home.isEmpty() ) {
+    result = QDir( QString::fromLocal8Bit( home ) );
+  }
+  else {
+    result = QDir::home();
+  }
+  const char * pathInHome = ".goldendict";
+#else
   result = QDir::home();
 #ifdef Q_OS_WIN32
   if ( result.cd( "Application Data/GoldenDict" ) )
@@ -2240,6 +2253,7 @@ QDir getHomeDir()
     pathInHome = xdgSubdirName;
   }
   #endif
+#endif
 #endif
 
   result.mkpath( pathInHome );
diff --git a/src/dict/dictionary.cc b/src/dict/dictionary.cc
index e18b43b3..8c2292cc 100644
--- a/src/dict/dictionary.cc
+++ b/src/dict/dictionary.cc
@@ -255,7 +255,7 @@ void Class::loadIcon() noexcept
 
 int Class::getOptimalIconSize()
 {
-  return 64 * qGuiApp->devicePixelRatio();
+  return 64;
 }
 
 bool Class::loadIconFromFileName( const QString & mainDictFileName )
diff --git a/src/tiff.cc b/src/tiff.cc
index d483af6e..2dec11c2 100644
--- a/src/tiff.cc
+++ b/src/tiff.cc
@@ -18,9 +18,10 @@ void tiff2img( std::vector< char > & data )
     QBuffer buffer( &ba ); // buffer doesn't own ba
     buffer.open( QIODevice::WriteOnly );
 
-    QSize screenSize = QApplication::primaryScreen()->availableSize();
     QSize imgSize    = img.size();
-    int scaleSize    = qMin( imgSize.width(), screenSize.width() );
+    QScreen * scr     = QApplication::primaryScreen();
+    QSize screenSize  = scr ? scr->availableSize() : imgSize;
+    int scaleSize     = qMin( imgSize.width(), screenSize.width() );
     img.scaledToWidth( scaleSize ).save( &buffer, "webp" );
 
     data.resize( ba.size() );
--
